From e66d44fbf641a96664a19fbbad1c873a603dfa67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hank Yeomans <hank@quorra.ah.local>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:13:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 23/51] kt_timeline: opt-in per-layer decode timeline +
 recorded-tensor dump (recipe T3.19a)

KT_TIMELINE=1 bakes external timing events (torch.cuda.Event(external=True))
into every breakable-graph capture at six points per MoE layer on the kt path
(start / export / gpu / sync / h2d / end) and records segment events plus
host clocks around each replay segment and eager break. Every replay writes a
"tick" (host t0/t1); every KT_TIMELINE_SAMPLE-th replay syncs and writes a
"step" record with per-segment GPU time, inter-segment gaps (the Engram
breaks), per-break host time and per-layer buckets (export, gpu_experts,
cpu_wait, h2d, combine, cpu_total) to KT_TIMELINE_DIR/timeline-rank{r}.jsonl.
The same capture copies hidden_states / topk_ids / topk_weights / kt output /
MoE output for KT_TIMELINE_DUMP_LAYERS (default 14,20) into private buffers
inside the graph and saves them after a sampled replay; eager decode-size
forwards of those layers are saved too (T3.16e(3) parity input).

kt_ep_wrapper._sync_timed mirrors kt-kernel 0.7.0.post4 BaseMoEWrapper.
sync_forward (sync_with_cuda_stream then copy_forward_output_to_device) so a
mark can sit between the wait and the H2D; the recipe's in-image test asserts
the installed kt still has that order. Falls back to sync_forward when
KT_FORCE_SYNC_SUBMIT=1.

With KT_TIMELINE unset every touched path is behaviour-identical: get_timeline
returns None, mark/dump stay None, and apply() takes the original sync()
branch. Streamed-prefill layers are not instrumented.

Measured on the qualified profile (recipe evidence/t319/a): GPU-event buckets
explain 98.9-99.7 % of the unsampled replay period at bs 1 and 4 on both
ranks; C1 41.37/39.15 wall tok/s (gate >= 39.0), C4 57.80/55.56, NLL 0 tokens
moved, consistency PASS, 0 NaN/Xid, EDAC 0/0.

Amp-Thread-ID: https://ampcode.com/threads/T-01a0c10b-a5f8-77fc-b238-7147d12ccf29
Co-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>
